note seed/host/container/capw.om: capset on a writable zero-version header: the kernel returns -22 and stores
note its preferred version 0x20080522 into the header (exit 0); capget on the same header then succeeds (exit 0).
note Any other outcome exits 1 (capset result), 2 (header bytes) or 3 (capget).
fn main to int
h = new uchar 32 0
r = capset h 0 32
if ne r -22
ret 1
end
if or ne get h 0 34 ne get h 1 5
ret 2
end
if or ne get h 2 8 ne get h 3 32
ret 2
end
k = capget h 0 32
if ne k 0
ret 3
end
ret 0
end
note gate-pools: uses capset on purpose: owner=seed/host/container/check.sh new-word acceptance or refusal qualification
note gate-pools: uses capget on purpose: owner=seed/host/container/check.sh new-word acceptance or refusal qualification
